{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Who is near to him.</b> But not a betrothed woman." "<b>To his mother and to his father.</b> The vav in place of 'or.' And likewise ולבנו ולבתו ולאחיו ולאחותו. If it says לאמו, what does it need to say ולאביו? — and what: his mother, who is subject to halitzah (and thus her identity is uncertain), behold he defiles himself for her; his father, who is not subject to halitzah — is it not logical that he should defile himself for him? Rather, had I only said thus: what his mother — certainly known, so too his father — certainly known; his father by presumption (that the father's identity is assumed certain), from where? Scripture says ולאביו. And if it said לאביו, I would have said: what — his father who is by presumption, behold he defiles himself for him; his mother who is certain — is it not logical that he defiles himself for her? Rather, unless I would say thus: what — his father who is not subject to halitzah, so too his mother who is not subject to halitzah. His mother who was subject to halitzah — from where? Scripture says לאמו ולאביו. Regarding an ordinary priest, it places father before mother, to tell you: it is not necessary — it is not necessary to say regarding his mother who is certain, that he defiles himself for her, but even regarding his father who is by presumption he defiles himself for him. And regarding the high priest, it places father before mother, to say: it is not necessary — it is not necessary to say regarding his father who is by presumption that he does not defile himself for him, but even his mother who is certain — he does not defile himself for her. ולבנו ולבתו — if it says לבנו ולבתו, what does it need לאמו ולאביו? And what: his son and daughter, regarding whom he is not obligated in the commandment of honor, behold he defiles himself for them; his father and mother, regarding whom he is obligated in honor — is it not logical that he defiles himself for them? Rather, had I only said לבנו ולבתו, I would say even if they are stillborn; Scripture says לאמו ולאביו — what his mother and father are viable, so too his son and daughter are viable; this excludes his stillborn son and daughter. What does it need לבנו ולבתו? Rather, because there is something in a son that is not in a daughter, and in a daughter something that is not in a son: the son — his father is obligated in him for the commandment, which is not so for a daughter; and the daughter — her father is entitled to her found objects, the work of her hands, and the annulment of her vows, which is not so for a son. Therefore it needs to say ולבתו." "<b>And to his sister.</b> If it says לאחיו ולאחותו and does not say לבנו ולבתו — what: his brother and sister, regarding whom he is not obligated in commandments, behold he defiles himself for them; his son and daughter, regarding whom he is obligated in commandments — is it not logical that he should defile himself for them? Rather, had I only said לאחיו ולאחותו — I would say even from his mother; Scripture says לבנו ולבתו — what his son and daughter who inherit, so too his brother and sister who inherit; this excludes his brother and sister from his mother who do not inherit. If it says לאחיו, what does it need to say <b>ולאחתו</b>? Rather, had it said לאחיו and not said <b>לאחתו</b>, I would have said: what — his brother whether older or younger he defiles himself for him, so too his sister whether older or younger he defiles himself for her; Scripture says <b>ולאחתו הבתולה</b> — younger and not older. And had it said ולאחותו and not said לאחיו, I would have said: what — his sister who is younger and not older he defiles himself for her, so too his brother the younger and not the older he defiles himself for him; Scripture says לאחיו — whether older or younger."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {1 "Reading מתחלל as the standard rabbinic term for a woman subject to חליצה (halitzah), rendered 'subject to halitzah,' and ודאית/בידוע/חזקה as her identity being 'certain' vs. 'by presumption.' The logic of the kal va-chomer arguments depends on this reading."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:14:06.825127576Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}